WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.320
India's Chariot 1-11b model cuts Indian text tokens by two and a half times while running on phones. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 247. Sakana's Namasu Rezener, 10 cents cash sharing decoder, and a cluster of agent sandboxes follow. Then things to try and on the horizon. Chariot Artificial Intelligence Private Limited launched the Chariot 1 Foundation model suite, Wollkult reported on November 26th at Bharat Mandapam in New Delhi,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.640
with mate-wise secretary S. Krishnan performing the launch under the India AI mission,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.580
and Cheriot sits among the opening four groups picked to build sovereign foundation models.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.620
The suite pairs an 11 billion-parameter mixture of experts' large language model, or LLM,

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.420
that activates 4 billion-parameters per token with a text-to-speech system,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.860
both trained from scratch in India, and it ships three sizes, 10.7 billion,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:03.480
1.7 billion and 745 million parameters for data center, laptop and smartphone deployment.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:10.900
The speech model covers English plus Hindi, Bengali, Marathi, Tamil, Telugu, Canada,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.340
Malayalam, Gujarati, Punjabi, and Odia, and it chooses pronunciation from context for

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:25.160
numbers, dates, currencies, URLs, and abbreviations, clearing over 97% verbalization accuracy against

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.680
the async TTS pronunciation benchmark.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:34.880
IndicShift tokenization covers 1,012 characters across 12 Indian scripts, and nested training

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.820
sped runs 38% on the same GPUs, while model loss barely moved.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.240
Another reported method cut training time by 62%.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.280
Co-founder Parth Sarthi stated that a nation of India's scale and diversity cannot depend

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.620
on AI built elsewhere, and work is already underway on a 70 billion parameter model,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.033
with a trillion parameter system as a longer term aim. Namasu Small, from Sikana AI,

00:02:01.373 --> 00:02:07.893
Mark Tech Post Details, is a 30B-A3B reasoning model built on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano,

00:02:08.453 --> 00:02:17.553
and averages 60.1 across 25 benchmarks. Nemotron 3 Super at 120 billion parameters sits at 56.2,

00:02:17.553 --> 00:02:22.673
so the smaller active parameter count beats a much larger dense counterpart on aggregate

00:02:22.673 --> 00:02:28.727
reasoning tasks. Speculative decoding for sparse attention LLMs gained an open source

00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:34.547
drafter called DeFly 2 from Tencent. And each drafter layer reuses the target's key value

00:02:34.547 --> 00:02:41.407
cache and top-k indexer picks, adding no draft key value memory. Serving throughput at 64k

00:02:41.407 --> 00:02:47.747
rises by as much as 81%, and because the drafter shares the target's cache, extra memory stays

00:02:47.747 --> 00:02:50.907
at zero while long-context generation still speeds up.

00:02:51.727 --> 00:02:57.207
An unfinished Google novel now has an ending written by a Russian AI model, Reuters reported,

00:02:57.807 --> 00:02:59.947
and literary observers gave mixed reactions.

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:04.967
Those reactions cited both what current models can do when they continue classic literary

00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:09.887
works and the cultural sensitivities of AI stepping into national literary heritage.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:16.820
Researchers introduced stable gated Delta Net 2, an archive paper sets out, using symmetric

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:22.540
Erasure and decay-regulated residual writing to bound recurrent state growth at O of square root T.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.040
Asymmetric Erase operators in the original gated delta net 2 design

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.720
had caused exponential state growth, and on models of about 1.6 billion parameters,

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:38.520
the new method lifted the 128K average ruler score by 6.80 points

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:45.700
in the recurrent setting and average accuracy across 9 downstream tasks by 0.62 points in the hybrid

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:51.691
setting. A two-stage projected cross-model chain of thought vector transfer method, lifted

00:03:51.691 --> 00:04:01.871
base student models by 10.37 to 21.98 accuracy points on GSM 8K and math, and by 3.23 to 9.65

00:04:01.871 --> 00:04:07.371
pass at one points on four-code generation benchmarks, with teacher and student both

00:04:07.371 --> 00:04:13.371
frozen. Stage 1 learns a task-level chain of thought vector in the teacher. Stage 2 trains

00:04:13.371 --> 00:04:17.551
only a lightweight linear projector that maps it into the student's residual space,

00:04:18.071 --> 00:04:21.791
and student adaptation needs no teacher outputs or intermediate traces.

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:27.242
Launched darkly demonstrated parallel AI agents running in cloud sandboxes,

00:04:27.602 --> 00:04:33.922
how a link reported, and those agents produce 44 code changes. Agent execution stays isolated

00:04:33.922 --> 00:04:40.582
while still posting measurable productivity gains on real engineering tasks. On-chain bench from Valerie,

00:04:40.582 --> 00:04:45.862
Hacker-noon details test how safely and reliably AI agents use crypto wallets.

00:04:46.342 --> 00:04:51.002
Wallet operations run under realistic threat models, with standardized scoring for

00:04:51.002 --> 00:04:52.562
agentic financial actions.

00:04:53.545 --> 00:04:58.545
Japan's Amata and Hitachi are building AI agents for autonomous control of factory equipment

00:04:58.545 --> 00:04:59.105
and robots.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:01.165
Biggo Finance reported.

00:05:01.845 --> 00:05:06.425
Their work targets real-time decision loops on industrial machinery without constant human

00:05:06.425 --> 00:05:06.945
oversight.

00:05:06.945 --> 00:05:07.045
right.

00:05:07.911 --> 00:05:10.751
Metano left stealth with a $12 million seed.

00:05:11.391 --> 00:05:15.771
FF News reported to unify AI agent security across the enterprise.

00:05:16.391 --> 00:05:20.931
That round is meant to put consistent policy enforcement and runtime controls on agents

00:05:20.931 --> 00:05:22.491
that operate inside companies.

00:05:23.271 --> 00:05:29.211
Orcaster gained upgrades at Econ, International Mining reported, plus a new mining AI agent

00:05:29.211 --> 00:05:34.391
that targets autonomous operation of heavy equipment and extends the platform's existing orchestration.

00:05:34.391 --> 00:05:35.185
development.

00:05:35.185 --> 00:05:40.725
Developers are being advised to add explicit validation of tool responses, tech gig reported,

00:05:41.245 --> 00:05:43.025
to prevent unsafe agent behavior.

00:05:43.605 --> 00:05:49.085
Skip that check and agents can act on malformed or malicious tool outputs, with security and

00:05:49.085 --> 00:05:50.545
correctness failures downstream.

00:05:51.585 --> 00:05:59.405
Puzzling Bench supplies 23,777 community verified puzzles, and archive paper describes, including

00:05:59.405 --> 00:06:04.765
a rolling post-cut-off slice and a multi-modal pilot for contamination-resistant evaluation

00:06:04.765 --> 00:06:10.025
of frontier models. Each item includes the author-accepted answer, a short reference,

00:06:10.625 --> 00:06:16.237
the author's hints, community tags, and the creation date. Mine defends without training

00:06:16.237 --> 00:06:21.857
and without tying itself to one attack, re-ranking retrieved content by mutual information and

00:06:21.857 --> 00:06:26.757
embedding variants. It sits at the front of accuracy security trade-offs on Inja Squad,

00:06:26.757 --> 00:06:33.137
Inge Trivia QA, LC Inge Squad, and Ingec Agent while adding the lowest latency on long

00:06:33.137 --> 00:06:39.717
contexts, evaluated on a new long-context benchmark averaging 4,032 words per context.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:45.650
In brief, smaller on-premise models let banks keep sensitive data in-house rather than

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.130
shipping it to outside providers.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:53.670
PYMNTS reported, cutting regulatory exposure while still running useful inference in controlled

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.290
environments.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:54.450
payments.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:07:02.390
Chat GPT generated stock selections, Chose Unreported, delivered a 22% gain, beating the S&amp;P 500.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:09.470
OpenAI adjusted GPT 6.2 output limits, Info World reported, shrinking tokens delivered

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:15.050
at the existing price so customers now get fewer generated tokens per request, with no change

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.170
in subscription cost.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:22.490
Lexi, described on archive, runs a large language model workflow that pulls in virtual data

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:27.990
room files, pulls out due diligence facts with provenance, and drafts report sections

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:32.970
while lawyers keep the final legal judgment, classifying documents under a configurable

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:39.190
taxonomy, assigning target entities, and surfacing supporting passages with page-level citations.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:45.270
Self-evolution methods raise goal completion on app world and skills bench, yet English

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:50.690
still outruns Urdu and code-switched input, with the widest misses on multi-step tasks,

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:57.090
An IRT IQA supplies aligned English, Urdu translated, and code-switched versions of four

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.470
existing data sets, checked by humans.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:05.880
Download the three chariot-1 sizes and measure token counts on Hindi or Tamil text against

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.100
your current tokenizer.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:14.100
Run Sakana Namasu small on the 25 benchmark suite you already use and compare against Nemotron

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:14.860
3 Super.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:20.820
Add mine's mutual information re-ranker to an existing retrieval augmented generation pipeline

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:25.160
and test on LC-INGE-SQAD long contexts.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.940
Evaluate Launch Darkly's parallel agent sandboxing

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.200
on a small internal code-change workflow.

